WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.180
The Ebisugawa family is 
supposedly a family that

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.170
split off from the Shimogamo 
family in the first place,

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.360
but the relationship between the two 
has been bad for a long time.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.680
To ease the long-standing antagonism,

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:19.740
<b>Electric Brandy</b>

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.930
Soichiro's younger brother Soun

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.740
married into the Ebisugawa family.

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.730
But at the time he hated even 
the sight of the Shimogamo family

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.430
and just kept adding more fuel to the fire,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.710
making the Shimogamo family feel like idiots.

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.480
Why Dad decided on Soun's youngest daughter

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.090
<b>Soichiro</b>

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.090
<b>Soun</b>

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.110
Ebisugawa Kaisei as my fiancée,

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.350
I'll never know.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.890
<b>Yasaburo</b>

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.890
<b>Kaisei</b>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.890
It seemed absolutely ridiculous.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:47.020
But after Dad died, Ebisugawa Soun

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.920
unilaterally canceled the engagement,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.900
enraging Mom, who was fond of her.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:01:00.410
By the way, my cousin's weird, 
un-tanuki-like name "Kaisei,"

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.520
was something Dad came up with.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.010
<b>Episode 9: 
Kaisei, Daughter of Ebisugawa</b>

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.570
How beautiful!

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.990
The leaves were pretty, but Benten--

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.790
she's just like a celestial maiden!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.950
Thanks, I'll treasure this.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.910
How's the tanuki hot pot prep going?

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.100
The tanuki hot pot?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:19.100
The one getting the tanuki 
for the Friday Fellows' hot pot

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.390
is you, I thought, right?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.470
Yeah, it's not going so well.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:29.070
If I get kicked out, I don't know 
how I'll explain it to my old man.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:35.280
The Friday Fellows have never had a 
year-end-bash without tanuki hot pot.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.120
The Friday Fellows should just cut that out.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.920
You can say that sort of thing 
because you're young.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:48.370
The adult world has various circumstances 
to take into account.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.460
The workings of human 
society are bizarre, huh.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.840
There are things it's better to not know.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.210
And the things you need to know, you'll 
end up learning at some point.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:05.180
Nothing better than something that gets 
settled before you realize it's an issue.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.810
Anyhow, I pray everything goes well.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.840
I'll do my best.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.480
You are late! We were worried!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.610
Venturing into his territory of my own 
will was actually not such a big deal.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.670
And?

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:28.330
The professor might fail to capture a tanuki.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.130
His eyes kept shifting.

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.290
Oh, great!

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.820
We can't drop our guard.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.470
There are still three weeks until their bash.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:39.160
You're looking awfully docile. 
What's up?

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:44.040
He's worried the Center Stone 
might still be angry.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.130
What?

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.540
But you know,

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.940
since the time you messed with him

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:54.930
he's been treated much better.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:00.790
I bet he's pleased.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.330
I feel bad for saying so, 
but I was also wondering

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:08.660
if he was really spending all day 
transformed into a stone.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.870
You're too easy on Yasaburo.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.580
If you say stuff like that, 
he might feel justified.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.260
Grilling the Center Stone, 
beg his pardon--

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.640
I didn't grill him; 
I smoked him out is all!

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.790
That's still terrible.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.570
You're late!

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.930
Sorry!

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.550
I'm Shimogamo Yaichiro. 
Could you step aside?

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:49.270
We can't just believe that. Prove you're 
a member of the Shimogamo family.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.470
What?!

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.700
Coming through, thanks.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:57.640
How do we know they're 
from the Ebisugawa family?

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.750
Prove it!

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.370
We're fine. Because we're great.

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.580
We're what's known as "versatile."

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:09.160
Amazing, Big Brother! I'm impressed 
you know a word like "versatile."

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.840
And besides that,

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:15.850
we don't stalk a family's precious 
daughter like <i>some</i>one.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.470
And that <i>some</i>one, well, 
it's <i>you</i>! Got it?

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.500
What are you talking about, you jerk?

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:23.950
When did I ever do something 
as shameless as that?

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:28.840
Father was troubled, saying it could 
have a bearing on her future.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.380
The engagement was canceled, 
but you still don't get it?

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:37.210
We don't need blood from the 
likes of the Shimogamo family!

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.660
Go to hell!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.040
Go to hell! Go to hell!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.540
Go to hell!

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.740
Go home!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.480
Why don't you go home?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.520
No, I'm telling <i>you</i> to go home!

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.890
Would you cut it out? 
How embarrassing.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:02.940
This is a shrine!

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:29.700
I was just thinking, but 
after a certain point

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.980
Father stopped visiting 
Prof. Akadama, didn't he?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.990
Even though they got along so well.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:38.860
But instead you and Yaichiro were going.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.080
Still, I'm sure the professor missed him.

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.950
He never said he wanted him to come,

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:48.570
but it was probably beneath 
his dignity so how could he?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.710
Prof. Akadama is also partly to blame.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:54.820
He's the one who brought 
Benten here, isn't he?

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:58.700
So never liked her.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.640
But back then Benten was 
pretty cute, I thought...?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:07.380
It's weird for such a great tanuki to 
get hung up on something like that.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.920
I guess it doesn't matter anymore 
if I mention this, so...

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:17.180
There was one time Prof. Akadama 
brought Benten to the forest.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:35.660
And So suddenly lost the 
ability to transform.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.480
He really worked at it,

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:41.700
but whenever Benten was around 
he would get anxious

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.500
and lose his transformation,

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.170
even though he was the best 
transformer in all of Kyoto.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.950
I never heard that story before.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:54.260
Well, he was keeping it a secret from 
everybody, including relatives.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:57.430
Only Prof. Akadama and Benten know.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:02.140
Kinda like how you lose your 
transformation when it thunders?

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.780
That's why So was avoiding Benten.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:13.200
Back then the professor was taking 
her everywhere he went, right?

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:17.040
So Yaichiro and I became the family reps?

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.770
Yep, exactly.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.490
If Prof. Akadama felt lonely,

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.340
he brought it on himself.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:31.250
I think So must have missed him, too.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.740
Close the gate!

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:47.550
Well then. Shimogamo Yaichiro and 
Ebisugawa Soun have announced

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:51.870
they will enter the race to 
become the new Nise-emon.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:55.510
Now we will formally

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:58.540
report this to the Center Stone.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.830
Silence!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:32.330
Moving on, in deciding 
the chief of tanuki society

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:38.700
it is customary to be graced with the 
presence of a Kurama tengu as a witness.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:43.620
However, we have received word from 
Teikinbo of the Kurama that due to

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:47.570
the ailing condition of his stomach, 
he will be unable to attend.

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.190
The meeting isn't for another three weeks.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:55.190
When we said that we'd like 
to invite another tengu,

00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:59.630
he said, "In that case, I'll 
concede to Yakushibo."

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.970
Therefore,

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:06.720
we'd like to invite Nyoigatake 
Yakushibo this time.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.230
Are there any objections?

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.300
I will take that as a no.

00:11:12.670 --> 00:11:15.590
Very well. The council will be held 
in the presence of the elders

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:18.080
the evening of December 26

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.330
at Sensuido in Kiyamachi.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.870
That is all for today. 
Everyone is dismissed.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.000
<b>Teramachi 
shopping district</b>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.000
<b>Daimaru</b>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.000
<b>Tsutaya Coffee</b>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.000
<b>Rokkakudo</b>

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.000
<b>Nishizaki Genemon's shop</b>

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.010
<b>December 22 (Sunday)</b>

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.770
I just heard from Yaichiro.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:53.210
Please get over to Prof. Akadama's place.

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.020
I'm a little busy at the moment.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:58.070
You're just warming your butt!

00:11:58.300 --> 00:12:01.850
A chilled bottom is the root 
of all illness, Mother.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.900
You gotta keep it really warm!

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:10.350
Apparently Prof. Akadama doesn't want to attend 
the meeting to decide who'll be Nise-emon.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.320
He's giving everyone a headache 
again with his whining.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:19.050
I thought since they said they'd like to 
invite him they had already run it by him?

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:24.240
No, this came up very suddenly. 
It's a problem for everyone.

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:29.470
So they said that the professor might listen 
if it were you, and asked me to find you.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.350
How convenient that they can expect so 
much of me when it suits their purposes.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.850
The professor and I don't have 
that kind of relationship.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:39.880
I said I would send you over 
to his place right away,

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:41.090
so please just go!

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.290
C'mon, hop to it!

00:12:43.290 --> 00:12:47.370
Got it, I'm going, I'm going!

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:52.620
Hello, I'm Yasaburo.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.920
Oh, Yasaburo is here.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.470
It's Yasaburo.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.880
Yes, hello.

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.420
It's Yasaburo!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.800
Yasaburo is here.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.940
'Scuse me, pardon me.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.120
Don't step on me, Yasaburo, 
for crying out loud.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.510
How's it going?

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.490
He won't budge an inch.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:15.390
We've brought additional offerings,

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.430
but now we're out of ideas.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.580
We've tried everything we possibly can.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:23.700
I can hear you, Yaichiro.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.350
Professor, Professor.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.510
I, Shimogamo Yasaburo, have come.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.020
For what purpose have you come?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.380
I don't remember calling you.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.600
There's no need to sulk about it.

00:13:42.600 --> 00:13:46.230
Why not make an appearance and think 
of it as an end-of-the-year party?

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.210
What a pain!

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:51.150
I can't deal with the thought of my 
drinks being ruined by tanuki hair.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:53.150
But I know you're actually 
happy to have been invited!

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:54.500
What?!

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.530
Yasaburo.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:03.370
Yes?

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.610
Go buy some Q-tips.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:10.650
When my ears are itchy I get irritable 
and whip up whirlwinds.

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.080
I really do!

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:16.930
Understood. I'll procure 
them with haste.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:20.460
About that tanuki meeting or whatever...

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.600
why do I have to go?

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:26.030
We do indeed humbly request your presence.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:29.080
It can't start without you.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:33.820
Tanuki from Kyoto and beyond 
will be waiting for your word.

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:39.650
Anyhow, this role is probably being forced on 
me because the Kurama thought it was a pain.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.730
To put it bluntly, that is correct.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.520
I figured it was something like that.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.720
"If we can just get whatever tengu 
happens to be on hand to come,

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:51.090
we can keep up appearances in a pinch."

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.770
That's the basic idea, huh.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.630
Is there even one tanuki amongst you

00:14:56.630 --> 00:15:00.190
who truly respects me?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.940
I wonder.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:07.370
I'll bet all those schmucks are sticking 
their tongues out at me in their hairball minds.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:12.710
Does such a great tengu 
as Nyoigatake Yakushibo

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:15.480
require the respect of hairballs?

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:20.920
Are you proud because tanuki respect you?

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.450
You're proud because you're respected?

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:26.180
I don't think so.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:30.160
The reason you're proud 
is that you're a tengu.

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:32.990
Tanuki and humans may 
stick out their tongues,

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:36.160
but you're a tengu because you're 
unquestionably great, isn't that right?

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:41.460
I will lock up what you 
said earlier deep inside.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.320
So please forget it.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:51.480
Tell them to prepare drinks and wait.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.210
If I feel like it, I'll do 
them a favor and go.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.990
Yessir.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.490
Yasaburo.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:02.840
You probably think this means I'll 
come, without a doubt, huh.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:06.800
Ah, I'd expect no less from you, Professor. 
You know what I'm thinking?

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:11.860
Of course I know what you 
hairballs are thinking.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.960
What a bunch of idiots.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:17.410
How'd it go?

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:18.600
How'd it go?

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:19.840
He'll come.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.130
Way to go!

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:22.910
Phew!

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.180
Nice job.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:26.790
Every tanuki has at least 
one good point.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.270
Gimme a break!

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:37.930
<b>Today: Hot Yuzu Bath 
"Everybody, let's warm up!"</b>

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.580
Guess I'll reheat my butt.

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:49.790
I hope he becomes Nise-emon.

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.740
Do your best again today, Yaichiro.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:57.330
He's wimpy when put on the spot

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:01.540
but if it's for the sake of Kyoto's tanuki,

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.910
whether through fire or water--

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.320
What a meaningless song!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:10.090
Huh? Kaisei?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:13.240
Did you to come relax 'n 
warm up your butt, too?

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:17.610
Don't talk about butts to 
a lady, you big perv.

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:21.900
M'lady, if you wish to avoid catching a 
cold, protect your hiney from the chill.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.850
Right, thanks.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:31.210
What a nice bath.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:34.660
It is a nice bath, huh. 
The yuzu is nice, too.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:35.940
Sure is.

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:39.220
I saw the Center Stone for 
the first time in a while.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.930
He's a stone, as usual.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:45.780
It's amazing he can stay 
transformed for so long.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:49.830
It'd be impossible for you, huh. At some 
point you'd lose your transformation.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.690
I could totally do it if I wanted to.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:56.860
I'm confident I would win against 
my big brother or our mother.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:18:00.390
There's no tanuki who can keep 
a transformation as well as me.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.610
By the way,

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.650
when are you planning on 
showing yourself to me?

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:08.480
Why should I?

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.120
You could pop over to the 
men's bath for a minute?

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:27.180
What a nice bath.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:30.840
What a nice bath.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:35.020
The Nise-emon will be selected 
next week; pretty soon, huh.

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.090
Yaichiro will not be it, I'm positive.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.490
Why not?

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.830
He's just not up to the task.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:47.480
And because of that my stupid old man 
intends to brush him aside and become Nise-emon.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:51.920
When it comes to caliber, Yaichiro's about 
neck and neck with my dumbass brothers.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.990
Even if he were the caliber of a 
rotten fish, he's my big brother!

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:56.750
Don't lump him in with those dumbasses!

00:18:56.750 --> 00:19:01.180
You numbskull! I'm not gonna 
let you insult my brothers!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.320
But you called them "dumbass brothers" yourself!

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:06.380
Who said that makes it okay for you?

00:19:06.380 --> 00:19:09.810
Don't get cocky, you airheaded 
double-numb-skull!

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:18.580
Anyways, tell Yaichiro to be careful.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.870
You know I wouldn't steer you wrong.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:25.840
What do you mean? Are those idiots trying to 
be clever again with their nonexistent smarts?

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:30.420
<i>Don't</i> call my brothers<i> idiots</i>, 
you rotten hairball!

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.290
But yeah, something like that.

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:39.360
I'm sure it's not much of a strategy anyways, 
but I'd be grateful if you tell me what it is.

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:45.670
Well, my idiot brothers have 
gotten more careful.

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:50.080
They're up to no good, but making 
sure I don't find out what.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.770
If you underestimate them, 
they'll get you.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:55.030
Ugh, those guys.

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:57.140
Don't get high 'n mighty 
like a tengu, Yasaburo.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:59.460
How can I be like a tengu?!

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:03.370
I'm a tanuki, geez. It's not 
like I'm Benten, either.

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:06.140
Don't talk to me about 
that rotten tengu!

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:10.810
Oh yeah, you've always 
hated her, huh.

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:15.930
I'd rather die than have to hear 
about that half-baked tengu.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.340
Besides that...

00:20:28.800 --> 00:20:30.340
What?

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:32.980
I'm sorry.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.510
Kaisei?

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:45.180
Those words, revealing a humble 
side of my ex-fiancée,

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:50.600
which she had never shown a hair of as far
 as I can remember, struck me as weird.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.100
<b>Terra Terrace</b>

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:56.330
Or more than weird, ominous.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:08.070
That's amazing!

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:12.100
Yashiro, you need to keep developing 
this talent of yours!

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:12.950
I will!

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:16.660
The day after the day after tomorrow 
is the Nise-emon election.

00:21:16.660 --> 00:21:18.660
What are you doing at such an important--

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:23.000
This is also a gathering to pray 
for your victory, you know.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.860
Have some fried chicken.

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:40.620
It's snowing!

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:49.820
I don't think the "I'm sorry" I heard 
from the women's bath like a sigh

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:54.610
was a simple apology.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:57.400
But if that's the case,

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:59.760
then what was it?

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:34.850
I'm a human being, 
I won't eat you alive.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:39.930
No wait, good grief. 
I'm a tanuki!

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>The Behind-the-Scenes 
Dealings of Ebisugawa Soun</b>
